  "major": "Social Studies Education for Teacher Licensure",
  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 Arkansas Tech University Catalog, 'Social Studies Education for Teacher Licensure' curriculum (pp. 179-181), a genuine institution-published sample plan ('The matrix below is a sample plan for all coursework required for this program'). This program combines a traditional history degree with all the necessary education courses to allow students to finish in four years. See the College of Education and Health (p. 248) page for additional requirements; for licensure, students must achieve the minimum score on the Praxis II Specialty Area and Principles of Learning and Teaching Tests as determined by the Arkansas Department of Education (see Admission and Retention to Teacher Education and Criteria for Internships, p. 248). Catalog footnote 1: see appropriate alternatives or substitutions in General Education Requirements (p. 75). Catalog footnote 2: students must complete HIST 2513 Sources and Methods in History and HIST 4963 Senior Seminar, or POLS 2513 Research Design and POLS 4963 Senior Seminar. Catalog footnote 3: must earn a grade of 'C' or better. Catalog footnote 4: SEED 4553 Classroom Application of Educational Psychology and SPED 4052 Educating Diverse and Exceptional Learners are part of the Residency A requirements in the completion of a yearlong residency experience per Arkansas Division of Elementary and Secondary Education (DESE) requirements; in the Residency A semester immediately prior to the student's last semester (Residency B), students must complete a minimum 270-hour field-experience component as part of the DESE requirements for teacher licensure. The COMM 2003 vs. COMM 2173, HIST 2513 vs. POLS 2513, POLS 3033/3123/3133/3143 select-one, and HIST/POLS 4963 slots are seeded as single choice slots per catalog; the HIST 2513/POLS 2513 choice must pair with the matching senior seminar per footnote 2. Machine prereqs omitted (prereq: []) — the curriculum page prints no per-course prerequisites. tccns mirrors the local ATU course code; transfer_confidence core_only.",
